id: pmc-txk1
title: List closed issues under Fixed only when a repair is recorded
description: "Require tracker repair evidence before classifying closed issues as Fixed; use neutral Closed entries for factual closures and omit non-change dispositions. Repro: pm-github-n0mm; classifier history: pmc-874d."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: changelog,classifier
created_at: "2026-10-20T10:13:29.451Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-20T10:40:18.819Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Real-shaped classifier table, historical incident repro, full snapshot, no-git stdin and tracker input, behavioural revert proof, unchanged npm and Bun release gates, regenerated own changelog."
comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-20T10:14:19.120Z",codex-agent,"Search found no existing evidence-based closure feature; pmc-874d is historical classifier precedence work. Design: for closed Issue/Bug/Bugfix/Defect records, explicit non-change dispositions in close_reason or resolution take precedence and are excluded. Other closures require linked files/tests, explicit affirmative repair wording in close_reason/resolution, or delivered/merged PR or commit evidence in resolution/actual_result/links; otherwise render Closed: title under Closed. Type/tag/title alone is not repair evidence. Features and Tasks retain existing classification. All projections use one selection policy; JSON reports non-change exclusions. Tracker data only; preserve existing release placement and prepend history. Fixtures will use sanitized SDK/fleet field shapes, including source closure timestamps and GitHub completion wording."
  "2026-10-20T10:20:22.684Z",codex-agent,"Focused regressions pass 57/57 (zero skipped): SDK/fleet-shaped files/tests, resolution/actual_result, merged PR/commit links, affirmative and negated repair statements, all non-change disposition spellings, incident repro, full historical snapshot, deterministic reversed input, preserved prepend history, and real SDK-created no-git tracker plus stdin under empty PATH. Policy refinement: non-change dispositions apply to every closed item type; Feature/Task category behavior otherwise stays unchanged. JSON exclusion count is across input before release/status filtering, making omitted administrative closures visible without claiming a release-specific count."
  "2026-10-20T10:24:30.951Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof in a disposable source copy, rebuilt before testing: reverting only needsNeutralClosure to the previous no-gate behavior fails 3/3 selected incident, full-snapshot and no-git regressions (0 pass). Reverting only isNonChangeClosure fails 6/6 selected disposition regressions (0 pass). The working source is untouched. The original classifier precedence suite passes 12/12 with explicit repaired fixtures. SDK fixture correction: create seeds use file/test string arrays; files objects are silently ignored by runCreate, so integration tests now seed through the documented singular options."
  "2026-10-20T10:32:46.712Z",codex-agent,"The first isolated-home full npm gate reached nine existing worker-readiness failures in test/generator-redos.test.ts (startup at 5000ms, before operation CPU measurement); the closure-evidence and no-git tests passed. This reproduces the separate pmc-redos-startup-231 issue. No parser budget, watchdog, source inventory or coverage threshold is changed. Trying an unchanged readiness control with process CPU affinity restricted to one available CPU, which also makes the Node test runner schedule files serially."
  "2026-10-20T10:40:18.819Z",codex-agent,"Final review tightened delivery references: bare resolved states, delivered issue references and issue-URL fragments are not merged-PR evidence. The classifier table passes 59/59; independent link-rendering controls pass 7/7 after repaired fixtures gained explicit resolution. Final source has the unchanged 5000ms worker startup, 250ms parser CPU and 5000ms operation watchdog, and unchanged 100 percent line/branch/function coverage thresholds. README section rules and release-note docs describe evidence, dispositions, neutral prefixes and exclusion-count scope."
